# Rule 2, by type (the linter's second stage, #1211): a constrained function
# template that no deny-rule refuses is instantiated at archetypes built from
# the shapes in its signature (archetypes.hpp, Appendix G.1 of the paper) and
# type-checked there.  A finding is a definition NOT admitted: its body uses
# something its signature does not promise, or at other types; a refusal, a
# witness that the definition is outside Jlt.  The other two rungs have rules
# of their own, so each is counted and gated apart: `undecided-by-type` (no
# verdict) and `admitted` (shown inside).
tool admit
